From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Anthony Fu (via agent)" <reg-github-bot@antfu.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:51:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add a host default worktree setup script

Projects without a worktree.setup in paseo.json get no setup in new
worktrees, so a host owner had to add the same paseo.json to every
project. The host config now stores optional default setup commands
(worktrees.defaultSetup in config.json), exposed as worktreeDefaultSetup in
the mutable daemon config; null clears them.

Worktree setup resolution falls back to these commands only when the
project's paseo.json leaves worktree.setup out entirely. The normalized
config turns an absent and an empty setup into the same [], so the raw
config decides; a project that declares any setup, even an empty one,
keeps its own. The fallback sits in getWorktreeSetupCommands, so worktree
creation and bootstrap both get it.

The app gates on the new server_info.features.worktreeDefaultSetup flag:
Host settings > Workspaces gets a one-command-per-line editor, and a
project's setup field says when the host default applies.

Fork-Change: F-4
